<!--
  A field of stars: three filled five-point stars of graded size.
  This shape has to dodge TWO look-alikes, so do not "simplify" it (D83):
    - One hollow outlined five-point star is the platform favorite/rating
      glyph. Three FILLED stars of unequal size is not - filled, plural and
      asymmetric are all load-bearing.
    - A large FOUR-point sparkle with smaller companions is the near-universal
      "generate with AI" glyph (Material auto_awesome, Gemini). Five points
      with straight shoulders, rather than four with pinched waists, is what
      keeps this an astronomical star field.
  Filled rather than stroked because stars are solid points of light, and
  because thin outlines at rail size (~30px) collapse into blobs.
-->
